<p class="faq-reskin__answer-text">Start by trimming any long hair down to stubble so the shaver can glide smoothly. You can shave wet or dry, but using warm water or shaving cream can help prevent irritation. Move the shaver in small, circular motions to get an even shave, and check for any rough spots you might have missed. When you're done, rinse your head with cool water to soothe your skin and clean your shaver so it's ready for next time. Need a full step-by-step guide? <a rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank" href="{%- for b in section.blocks -%}{%- if b.settings.slot == 's1615' -%}{{ b.settings.link | default: '#' }}{%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}" data-atl-slot="s1615" style="{%- for b in section.blocks -%}{%- if b.settings.slot == 's1615' -%}{{ b.settings.style }}{%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}">{%- for b in section.blocks -%}{%- if b.settings.slot == 's1615' -%}{{ b.settings.text | newline_to_br }}{%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}</a>.</p>
